# P9 · Practice operations and engagement · Week 65 onward · R9 Ongoing
# Source: comparison with DentalERP (github.com/abinauv/dental-erp, MIT), 17 Nov 2026. Only gaps with no ticket elsewhere are here; see the phase "Not in this phase" line.
# DentalERP is Next.js + Prisma: its files are a reference for schema and flow. Backend is rewritten in C#; UI is rebuilt on @medvya/ui (AGENTS.md: no second component library). Copied code keeps the MIT notice.
# exit: 1 per feature: adoption target agreed before build
# exit: 2 each epic demonstrated on the real stack in English and Arabic, axe clean
# nfr:  1 P8-001 intake per feature
# nfr:  2 no patient health detail in messages, calendar entries, exports or AI prompts beyond need
# pkg:  1 minor-version release notes per feature
# dep:  1 DentalERP reference only; copied code keeps its licence notice
# dep:  2 DLT templates and marketing opt-in before campaigns

@epic MDV-P9-E01 | Stock and suppliers | P9-01 | The clinic knows what it has, what expires and what to reorder, without a spreadsheet.
@epic MDV-P9-E02 | External lab send-outs | P9-02 | A test sent to an outside lab is tracked until its report is in the results inbox.
@epic MDV-P9-E03 | Payment plans | P9-03 | A patient can pay a large balance in agreed instalments, and the desk sees what is due.
@epic MDV-P9-E04 | Staff time and calendars | P9-04, P9-06 | Rota, attendance and leave in one place; doctors see their clinic day in their own calendar.
@epic MDV-P9-E05 | Patient engagement | P9-05 | The clinic can reach consenting patients, hear their feedback and reward loyalty, within the messaging rules.
@epic MDV-P9-E06 | Operational AI | P9-07 | Owners and the desk get forecasts and answers as drafts they can check, never automatic actions.

=== MDV-P9-001
title: P9 intake: adoption target, evidence and rules check for each P9 feature
type: Chore
epic: MDV-P9-E01
prd: P9-01, P9-02, P9-03, P9-04, P9-05, P9-06, P9-07
covers: exit:1, nfr:1, nfr:2, pkg:1, dep:1, dep:2
priority: MUST
roles: Founder
labels: governance
estimate: 0.5
weeks: 65
depends: MDV-P8-001
confidence: 85 | Same process as P8-001.
sources: DentalERP comparison (17 Nov 2026); PRD P9
desc:
Run the P8-001 intake for every P9 feature: who asked for it, the adoption target, and the rules that apply (DLT and opt-in for campaigns; NMC and DHA rules on patient inducements for loyalty points; regulatory class for any AI forecast). Record the DentalERP licence terms once for the whole phase.
ac:
- Each P9 ticket links an approved intake record before work starts.
- The DentalERP MIT notice is recorded in docs/compliance with the files it applies to, if any code is copied.
- Release notes per feature use the P8 minor-version template.

=== MDV-P9-002
title: Stock items: categories, units, reorder level and locations (Inventory module)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P9-E01
prd: P9-01
priority: SHOULD
roles: Owner, Practice admin
labels: inventory, stock
estimate: 3
weeks: 65
depends: MDV-P9-001
confidence: 65 | New module; DentalERP schema shows the shape.
sources: DentalERP prisma/schema.prisma (InventoryCategory, InventoryItem); app/api/inventory; app/(dashboard)/inventory; components/inventory/item-form.tsx
desc:
Creates the planned Inventory module (README): stock items with category, unit, pack size, reorder level and the location that holds them. Settings → Stock lists, adds and edits items.
ac:
- An admin can add, edit and retire an item; a retired item keeps its history.
- Each new property carries a data classification; tenant isolation tests cover the new tables.
- Quantities are decimals with a unit; prices are integer minor units with currency (AGENTS.md 3.4).
- Checked in English and Arabic, axe clean.
notes:
- Pick up from DentalERP: field list of `InventoryItem` and `InventoryCategory` in prisma/schema.prisma; screen flow of app/(dashboard)/inventory. Data to take: none (its categories are dental only).

=== MDV-P9-003
title: Batches and expiry: receive with batch and expiry, use first-expiring first, block expired
type: Story
epic: MDV-P9-E01
prd: P9-01
priority: SHOULD
roles: Practice admin, Nurse
labels: inventory, stock, safety
estimate: 2
weeks: 66
depends: MDV-P9-002
confidence: 70 | Simple rules; DentalERP has the same model.
sources: DentalERP prisma/schema.prisma (InventoryBatch)
desc:
Each receipt records batch number, expiry and quantity. Using stock takes the first-expiring batch unless the user picks one. An expired batch cannot be used.
ac:
- Using stock defaults to the batch that expires first.
- An expired batch is shown as "Expired" in words and cannot be logged as used.
- Batch and expiry show on every movement.
notes:
- Pick up from DentalERP: `InventoryBatch` fields.

=== MDV-P9-004
title: Stock movements: receive, use, adjust and transfer, with reasons and audit
type: Story
epic: MDV-P9-E01
prd: P9-01
priority: SHOULD
roles: Practice admin, Nurse
labels: inventory, stock, audit
estimate: 2
weeks: 66
depends: MDV-P9-003
confidence: 70 | Ledger pattern exists in billing (P4-012).
sources: DentalERP prisma/schema.prisma (StockTransaction); app/api/inventory
desc:
Every change in quantity is a movement (receive, use, adjust, transfer between locations) with a reason, a person and a time. The on-hand quantity is the sum of movements, never edited directly.
ac:
- On-hand equals the sum of movements, tested under concurrent use.
- An adjustment needs a reason; adjustments are on the audit log.
- A transfer moves the same batch between two locations in one step.
notes:
- Pick up from DentalERP: `StockTransaction` types. Do not copy its direct quantity update; Medvya uses an append-only ledger.

=== MDV-P9-005
title: Suppliers and purchase orders: draft, send, receive in part or in full
type: Story
epic: MDV-P9-E01
prd: P9-01
priority: SHOULD
roles: Owner, Practice admin
labels: inventory, purchasing
estimate: 3
weeks: 67
depends: MDV-P9-004
confidence: 65 | Standard flow; printing uses the QuestPDF family (ADR-018).
sources: DentalERP prisma/schema.prisma (Supplier, SupplierItem, PurchaseOrder, PurchaseOrderItem)
desc:
A supplier list with the items each supplies and their price. A purchase order moves Draft → Sent → Part received → Received or Cancelled. Receiving creates batches (P9-003) and receive movements (P9-004).
ac:
- Receiving part of an order leaves the rest open; receiving all closes it.
- A sent order prints or exports as PDF with clinic, supplier, items and quantities.
- Supplier GSTIN (India) or TRN (UAE) is validated by format.
notes:
- Pick up from DentalERP: the four models above and the status list.

=== MDV-P9-006
title: Low-stock and expiry alerts in the notification centre
type: Story
epic: MDV-P9-E01
prd: P9-01
covers: exit:2
priority: SHOULD
roles: Practice admin, Owner
labels: inventory, notifications
estimate: 1
weeks: 67
depends: MDV-P9-004, MDV-P9-003
confidence: 75 | Reuses the job runner and notification centre.
sources: DentalERP app/api/cron/inventory/route.ts; prisma/schema.prisma (StockAlert)
desc:
A daily job raises one alert per item below its reorder level and per batch expiring within 30 days (configurable), shown in the notification centre for admins.
ac:
- An alert is raised once and cleared when the stock is back above the level or the batch is used up.
- The expiry window is a clinic setting.
notes:
- Pick up from DentalERP: the rules in app/api/cron/inventory/route.ts.

=== MDV-P9-007
title: External lab list and send-out orders from investigation orders
type: Story
epic: MDV-P9-E02
prd: P9-02
priority: SHOULD
roles: Doctor, Nurse, Receptionist
labels: lab, orders
estimate: 2
weeks: 68
depends: MDV-P9-001, MDV-P2-018
confidence: 65 | Manual tracking only; HL7 feeds stay in P7-007.
sources: DentalERP prisma/schema.prisma (LabVendor, LabOrder, LabOrderHistory); app/api/lab-orders; app/api/lab-vendors; components/lab/lab-order-editor.tsx
desc:
A clinic list of outside labs. An ordered investigation (P2-018) can be sent out to a lab: sample, sent date, expected date. Status Sent → Received by lab → Reported, with history. The same lab list serves dental lab work (P8-018).
ac:
- A send-out shows only the data the lab needs on its print or export.
- Each status change is recorded with who and when.
- Overdue send-outs (past expected date) are listed for the desk.
notes:
- Pick up from DentalERP: `LabVendor` fields, `LabOrderHistory` pattern, status list of `LabOrderStatus`. Its work types are dental; pathology tests come from P2-018 instead.

=== MDV-P9-008
title: Returned lab report goes into results intake
type: Story
epic: MDV-P9-E02
prd: P9-02
covers: exit:2
priority: SHOULD
roles: Nurse, Doctor
labels: lab, results
estimate: 1.5
weeks: 68
depends: MDV-P9-007, MDV-P4-014
confidence: 70 | Builds on the P4-014 identity match.
sources: DentalERP prisma/schema.prisma (LabOrderDocument)
desc:
Uploading the returned report on a send-out passes it through results intake (P4-014) with the send-out already matched, and marks the send-out Reported.
ac:
- The report reaches the doctor's results inbox linked to the order.
- A report uploaded to the wrong send-out can be moved, with the move audited.

=== MDV-P9-009
title: Payment plan on an invoice balance: instalments, due dates and a printed schedule
type: Story
epic: MDV-P9-E03
prd: P9-03
priority: SHOULD
roles: Receptionist, Owner, Patient
labels: billing, payment-plan
estimate: 3
weeks: 69
depends: MDV-P9-001, MDV-P4-004, MDV-P4-009, MDV-P4-011
confidence: 60 | Interacts with dues and receipts; needs an accountant's view on India/UAE wording.
sources: DentalERP prisma/schema.prisma (PaymentPlan, PaymentPlanSchedule); app/api/payment-plans
desc:
The desk turns an invoice balance into a plan: number of instalments, first due date and frequency, or custom amounts. The schedule prints for the patient to sign. No interest or fees in v1.
ac:
- Instalments sum exactly to the balance in minor units (the last one takes the remainder).
- The plan and the patient's acceptance are recorded with who and when.
- A plan is not a loan: the printed wording is approved by the P4-031 accountant.
notes:
- Pick up from DentalERP: the two models and the split logic in app/api/payment-plans. Check its rounding; Medvya uses integer minor units.

=== MDV-P9-010
title: Instalment payments, overdue reminders and plan close
type: Story
epic: MDV-P9-E03
prd: P9-03
covers: exit:2
priority: SHOULD
roles: Receptionist
labels: billing, payment-plan, reminders
estimate: 2
weeks: 69
depends: MDV-P9-009, MDV-P1-032
confidence: 70 | Reuses payments and the reminder pipeline.
sources: DentalERP app/api/payment-plans/[id]
desc:
A payment against the invoice settles the oldest open instalment first. Overdue instalments show on the dues list and send a balance reminder with no clinical detail. The plan closes when paid or is cancelled with a reason.
ac:
- Reminders respect the patient's consent and carry no clinical detail.
- Cancelling a plan returns the remaining balance to ordinary dues.

=== MDV-P9-011
title: Staff shifts and rota per location
type: Story
epic: MDV-P9-E04
