desc:
A weekly rota for each location: who works which shift. Doctors keep their schedule templates (P1-011); the rota shows them read-only beside other staff.
ac:
- A shift cannot overlap another shift of the same person.
- The rota prints for the staff room without phone numbers.

=== MDV-P9-012
title: Attendance: clock in and out, corrections approved by an admin
type: Story
epic: MDV-P9-E04
prd: P9-04
priority: COULD
roles: Practice admin, Nurse, Receptionist
labels: staff, attendance
estimate: 2
weeks: 70
depends: MDV-P9-011
confidence: 60 | Labour-law record keeping varies; intake decides scope.
sources: DentalERP prisma/schema.prisma (Attendance); app/api/staff/attendance
desc:
Staff clock in and out on the clinic app. A missed or wrong entry is corrected by request and approved by an admin. A monthly attendance sheet exports as CSV.
ac:
- A correction keeps the original entry and records who approved it.
- No location tracking; clock-in is from a signed-in clinic session only.

=== MDV-P9-013
title: Staff leave requests and approval; approved doctor leave feeds the schedule
type: Story
epic: MDV-P9-E04
prd: P9-04
priority: COULD
roles: Practice admin, Doctor, Nurse, Receptionist
labels: staff, leave
estimate: 2
weeks: 70-71
depends: MDV-P9-011, MDV-P1-012
confidence: 65 | P1-012 already handles leave as a schedule exception.
sources: DentalERP prisma/schema.prisma (Leave); app/api/staff/leaves
desc:
Staff request leave; an admin approves or declines. Approved doctor leave becomes a P1-012 schedule exception, which re-offers affected appointments.
ac:
- Approved doctor leave creates the schedule exception once (idempotent).
- Declining needs a reason.

=== MDV-P9-014
title: Calendar sync: a doctor's appointments as busy blocks in Google or Outlook
type: Story
epic: MDV-P9-E04
prd: P9-06
covers: exit:2
priority: COULD
roles: Doctor
labels: calendar, integrations, privacy
estimate: 3
weeks: 71
depends: MDV-P9-001
confidence: 55 | OAuth app reviews by Google and Microsoft take time.
sources: DentalERP lib/services/google-calendar.ts; lib/services/outlook-calendar.ts; app/api/integrations; prisma/schema.prisma (CalendarIntegration)
desc:
One-way publish: each appointment of the doctor appears as "Busy · Medvya" with time only. No patient name, reason or location detail leaves Medvya. The doctor connects and disconnects from their account page.
ac:
- A published event contains no patient data (tested).
- Disconnecting deletes the published events and the stored tokens.
- Tokens are stored encrypted with Key Vault keys.
notes:
- Pick up from DentalERP: the OAuth and event calls in the two service files. Remove anything that writes patient names into events.

=== MDV-P9-015
title: Patient segments: saved filters for campaigns and reports
type: Story
epic: MDV-P9-E05
prd: P9-05
priority: COULD
roles: Owner, Practice admin
labels: crm, segments
estimate: 2
weeks: 72
depends: MDV-P9-001, MDV-P4-029
confidence: 60 | Must read from the PHI-safe reporting store.
sources: DentalERP app/api/crm/segments; app/(dashboard)/crm; lib/ai/skills/patient-segmentation.ts
desc:
A segment is a saved filter: last visit, age band, location, service used, outstanding balance, marketing consent. It shows a count and, to admins, the list.
ac:
- Diagnoses and clinical notes are not offered as filters.
- Counts under 5 are shown as "fewer than 5" outside the patient list.

=== MDV-P9-016
title: Campaign messages to a segment with consent, quiet hours, DLT template and opt-out
type: Story
epic: MDV-P9-E05
prd: P9-05
priority: COULD
roles: Owner, Practice admin
labels: crm, messaging, compliance
estimate: 3
weeks: 72
depends: MDV-P9-015, MDV-P1-045
confidence: 50 | Blocked on DLT (P1-045) in India; UAE advertising rules need a check.
sources: DentalERP app/api/communications/sms/bulk; app/api/communications/templates; app/api/communications/automations; lib/services/template.service.ts
desc:
Send a templated message to a segment, now or scheduled. Only patients with marketing consent receive it. India promotional messages go out only 9 AM to 9 PM and use an approved DLT template; every message has an opt-out.
ac:
- A patient without marketing consent is never sent a campaign (tested).
- A scheduled send outside 9 AM to 9 PM (India) waits until 9 AM.
- Opt-out takes effect before the next send and is recorded.
notes:
- Pick up from DentalERP: the 9 AM to 9 PM rule and template placeholders. Medvya reminder consent and marketing consent stay separate.

=== MDV-P9-017
title: Patient feedback after a visit: short survey and results per doctor
type: Story
epic: MDV-P9-E05
prd: P9-05
priority: COULD
roles: Patient, Owner
labels: feedback, survey
estimate: 2
weeks: 73
depends: MDV-P9-001, MDV-P1-032
confidence: 65 | Small; reuses messaging.
sources: DentalERP prisma/schema.prisma (Survey, SurveyResponse); app/api/communications/surveys; app/api/communications/feedback/analytics
desc:
After a completed visit, a consenting patient gets a link to a two-question survey (rating and comment). The owner sees results per doctor and per month.
ac:
- The link carries no patient data and expires after 14 days.
- Results with fewer than 5 responses are not shown per doctor.

